{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322826-looking-for-novel-interesting-ways-to-use-bureaucracy-in-my-game","id":1322826,"title":"Looking for novel/interesting ways to use Bureaucracy in my game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-07T13:38:23-07:00","id":1322826,"title":"Looking for novel/interesting ways to use Bureaucracy in my game.","content":"The title's pretty self-explanatory, but I'm not the most creative and so when it comes to how to use it, I struggle to figure out how beyond the most basics. Bribe people, make money, evaluate items, skip red tape (for some reason, I still haven't encountered an instance where it'd matter). <br /> <br /> For some context to help, the game setting and character using it are thus: We're in nexus, we're new exalts, and we were hella dumb and went blazing anima more than once and are now trying to hide within the cities underbelly as we've acquired enemies on a large and local scale. Criminal gangs we've run out of town, local dragon-blooded, and a few minor gods who hate that one of our exalts love of biological warfare (plague). <br /> <br /> My character is something of an idiot savant, with 1 intelligence, eidetic memory, and who invested hugely into attributes overall. Bureaucracy 4 at the moment and a ton of free-floating exp to spread around as needed for charms and the like. What interesting things could I do with bureaucracy to help us?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T13:50:11-07:00","id":1322827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322826-looking-for-novel-interesting-ways-to-use-bureaucracy-in-my-game#post1322826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title's pretty self-explanatory, but I'm not the most creative and so when it comes to how to use it, I struggle to figure out how beyond the most basics. Bribe people, make money, evaluate items, <b>skip red tape (for some reason, I still haven't encountered an instance where it'd matter)</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>One example that springs immediately to mind is the Council of Entities. Individuals on the Council have been known to take bribes to put a Civility on the books, or to strike out a pre-existing one.<br /> <br /> \u200bLet's say that normally it takes the better part of a day for your bribe to get a rule added to the Incunabulum; with Speed the Wheels, you can get it done in <i>minutes</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou then use Indolent Official Charm to slow down the overturning Civility you <i>know</i> is coming. It takes them a <i>week</i> to actually implement the rule that excises yours, giving you seven days of profit as your gang is the only one permitted to sell hippo ivory during daylight hours (or whatever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-07-2019, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-08T07:25:54-07:00","id":1322959,"title":"","content":"One thing to know about Bureaucracy is it is an engine to fulfill goals. <br /> <br /> So, what are your goals in the game? <br /> <br /> Want to cause trouble for your enemies? Research where their weak points are and make life difficult for them. For criminals, you can improve the local authorities. For DB nobility, figure out their businesses/investments and tank them.<br /> <br /> Acquire goods/resources? Open a business, take over the black market, set up a shell company if you are already exposed as Anathema.<br /> <br /> Make the government more Solar friendly? Find out who are you biggest enemies and destroy them. Find the skeletons in their closet or make them look incompetent. Find allies to replace them and manipulate the bureaucracy to make your allies look good.<br /> <br /> Some of these may require Investigation, Larceny, Social to support your Bureaucratic actions, but that is why you have a circle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T02:50:34-07:00","id":1324172,"title":"","content":"I think that one thing to help with assigning tasks to Bureaucracy is to imagine what a society keeps official records of, and how that information can be useful.<br /> <br /> The non-fiction Treason by the Book recounts an incident in 17th century Qing China in which, upon the authorities apprehending an anti-Manchu dissident, there was a very significant mobilisation of bureaucracy in order to determine the identities of various people whom the dissident had had contact with, in order to eliminate a number of people suspected on such sentiments. This involved combing records to find names based on a rough description of time and place several years ago, and then using that info to find their current residences.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying one necessarily needs to go so authoritarian with it, but it's a picture of how such things can work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T09:16:01-07:00","id":1324216,"title":"","content":"Quoth Vance:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Roll (Perception + Bureaucracy) to assess the manpower, supplies, or financial resources of an organization<br /> Roll (Intelligence + Bureaucracy) to know who in an organization you need to talk to get [task x] done<br /> Roll (Intelligence + Bureaucracy) to know how to report a crime to authorities in a way that gets an immediate response, rather than it just being thrown on a pile somewhere. <br /> Roll (Manipulation + Bureaucracy) to manage funds in a deceptive way, like keeping a Ponzi scheme running or cooking your books.<br /> Roll (Intelligence + Bureaucracy) to understand the finer points of the law or a local economy.<br /> Etc. etc. </div> </div> </div>While this isn't everything you're asking for, outlining specific sorts of actions you can do with Bureaucracy may help with the bigger picture of what you can do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T04:37:26-07:00","id":1325204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322826-looking-for-novel-interesting-ways-to-use-bureaucracy-in-my-game#post1322826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title's pretty self-explanatory, but I'm not the most creative and so when it comes to how to use it, I struggle to figure out how beyond the most basics. Bribe people, make money, evaluate items, skip red tape (for some reason, I still haven't encountered an instance where it'd matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>the skipping the red tape problem is mostly a fault with our vision of the world. Last year I visited the shogun palace in Japan, where there are many I information on who and how could talk and an audience with the shogun in Edo period. And it was almost no one. Having the possibility to speak with a king, emperor, or any kind of ruler should be hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12370-lddm84","name":"LDDM84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T06:47:17-07:00","id":1325230,"title":"","content":"Don't forget Stamina+Bureaucracy to survive red-tape when dealing with Yu-Shan and the lesser spirit courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T07:14:31-07:00","id":1325237,"title":"","content":"I think this is one of the most Exalted titles i have ever seen on a topic.<br /> <br /> You could also use it to hinder reports being sent to the Blessed isle to prevent a Wyld Hunt being formed, muddy up the information so to say. Use it to cover your trails so to say.<br /> <br /> Another tip is to look at how VtM uses basically the same to control cities, Sheriffs use it to keep the masquerade, arrest people who have seen things, ensure your haven are not disturbed in times you dont want it, ensure that the cops are open for bribes.<br /> <br /> There are no reason you cant take the same ideas into Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2610-lycaniz","name":"lycaniz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T02:48:47-07:00","id":1326921,"title":"","content":"Here are some things the eclipse known as Mako Li, <i>Heaven's Golden Fan</i> did during his time in Creation. Mako Li had 0 combat charms, maxed out Charisma, Appearance, Socialize, Bureacracy, Integrity and whatever other low hanging celestial fruit he could grab. Mostly infernal charms. Anyway, he:<br /> <br /> Taught Tea Ceremony to the Sister in Law of the Head of the Wyld Hunt in the Scavenger Lands<br /> Doubled the amount of supplies and speed of logistics for the Wyld Hunt<br /> Sent the Wyld Hunt 500 miles in the wrong direction<br /> Hid 3 new Solars from the Wyld Hunt<br /> Orchestrated the building of a secret fort temple to Sol Invictus<br /> Gossiped with said Sister in Law about how impossible such a rumored Fortress would be<br /> Imitated the driver of the Head of the Wyld Hunt<br /> Made said driver a spy against his will<br /> Encouraged a Pirate Armada to attack the treasure fleets of the Scavenger Land tributes<br /> Helped the Realm navy attack said pirates<br /> Organized rebels in a dramatic last stand against the Wyld Hunt<br /> Helped the Wyld Hunt break the siege of the rebels fort<br /> traded away the dead bodies of several hundred realm soldiers and a dozen DBs to a Fae Queen. <br /> Got Mask of Winters to attack the Fae queen. <br /> took a 20 year break because he fucked up that last bit really bad<br /> grew flowers in the literal shadow of the Abomination in Thorns. <br /> Married an Abyssal. <br /> Learned Sidereal Martial Arts in a single day. <br /> Turned an Abyssal into 3 ducks<br /> Shot said ducks. <br /> <br /> All but the last 4 are Socialize and Bureaucracy. There's a joke in the Vatican that the most informed person amongst all Catholics is <i>the Pope's driver</i>, because he goes everywhere, knows who visits His Holiness, has unrestricted access to basically everything. Under that logic I made allies out of the driver of the carriage of the Wyld Hunt Leader and his Sister in Law (who he was having an affair with), making Mako Li the single most informed person in the whole of the East. The Supplies, Pirates, War, etc were all to distract and weaken the Wyld Hunt while personally remaining in their good graces (after all, Mako DID get them more material than anyone else, faster and cheaper to boot. Its not his fault he was given bad intel about where to send it, wink wink). Things didnt go smooth at the end, but Mako kept the Wyld Hunt chasing wild sheep for 3 seasons. <br /> <br /> And that's how you use Bureaucracy (and get rich doing it- I got up to Wealth 2!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}